{"name":"Stunning Shade","hex":"#676064","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stunning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an effect that stuns.","Exceptionally beautiful or attractive."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of stun"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stunning"},{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stunning","blocks":[{"text":"Stunning is the process of rendering animals immobile or unconscious, with or without killing the animal, when or immediately prior to slaughtering them for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Medieval_pig_slaughter.jpg/330px-Medieval_pig_slaughter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stunning","wikidata":"Q7628762"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/37/Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg/500px-Richardson%27s